`,a.jsxs(e.p,{children:["Builds three models (multi-head, grouped-query with four KV heads, and latent attention) and forwards each without a window and with a window of ",s(B.window),", on each of the four backends. The model is ",s(m.dModel)," wide with ",m.nHeads," heads of ",m.headDim,", wider than the course model, so its matrix multiplications give the GPU enough work. Its weights are random, because nothing trains. Each of the 24 points takes ",m.warmup," untimed and ",m.repeats," timed forwards at batch ",m.batchSize," × ",s(m.sequenceLength)," tokens in bf16. A dense arm reaches the kernel without a mask, so the backend applies causality itself. A windowed arm carries the band as an explicit mask, because SDPA has no window argument. The same job then runs the decode steps and the sink evaluation below, and draws ",a.jsx(e.code,{children:"comparison.png"}),"."]}),`
