`,a.jsxs(e.p,{children:["The first table is arithmetic from the configuration, so yours should match it exactly. Cache elements are the values one token stores in one layer. The attention FLOPs are for one forward at batch ",m.batchSize," × ",s(m.sequenceLength),": semantic counts the query-key pairs the mask keeps, realized the whole square a kernel multiplies when it cannot skip masked pairs. FLOPs per byte is the forward's arithmetic intensity: model FLOPs, whose attention term is the semantic one, per byte of the exercise's traffic model. In that model every weight crosses memory once per sequence of ",s(m.sequenceLength)," tokens, and each token adds its stored cache in every layer."]}),`
