`,a.jsxs(e.li,{children:[a.jsx(e.code,{children:"FLASH_ATTENTION"})," serves both dense arms that are not latent attention, which reach it without a mask. It refuses the windowed arms, which need the band as an explicit mask, and latent attention, whose query and key are wider than its value."]}),`
`,a.jsxs(e.li,{children:["The window of ",s(B.window)," cuts the semantic attention work from ",X(B.denseSemantic)," to ",X(B.windowSemantic),", yet each windowed arm runs ",r(B.slowdown.min)," to ",r(B.slowdown.max)," slower than its dense twin on the faster fused backend. The kernel multiplies the whole square of an explicit mask, while the dense arm's masked half is skipped. A window pays only on a kernel that skips its tiles, as the window-tradeoff run below shows."]}),`
`,a.jsxs(e.li,{children:["Every point lies far above the ridge, at ",s(Math.round(v.intensity.min))," to ",s(Math.round(v.intensity.max))," FLOPs per byte, yet the best eager point reaches ",r(v.bestEager,1)," MFU. A large matrix multiplication reaches ",r(v.ceiling,1)," on this card, which runs under a ",de," W power limit instead of the default ",Te," W."]}),`
