`,a.jsxs(e.p,{children:["No job of its own: the ",a.jsx(e.code,{children:"compare.py"})," job above times one decode step of attention in one layer, one new query for each of ",A.batch," sequences, against caches of ",s(P[0]),", ",s(P[1])," and ",s(P[2])," positions. Multi-head and grouped-query attention read cached keys and values. Latent attention reads its cache two ways. Absorbed, each head's query takes the key up-projection and the output takes the value up-projection, so every head attends over the latent itself. Unabsorbed, every head's keys and values are rebuilt from the whole cache on every step. The step is built from plain matrix multiplications, and ",a.jsx(e.code,{children:"comparison.png"})," draws it in its last panel."]}),`
